course: dictionary
lesson: 2221
title: Words for places and people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A courtroom is a room in a law court where trials and hearings take place. «Then we jump to a courtroom.» The word tells you the place is a room inside a court, so it is not just any room.
explain: Look at the words around it. A courtroom has places for the judge, the jury, the lawyers, the person accused and the public. If a story mentions a judge and a jury, you can guess the setting is a courtroom.
explain: «Every night at eight o'clock Kai's house turned into a courtroom.» Kai's house is not a real court. The family is playing a game, so the word is being used in a playful way, for a pretend trial.
fact: A courtroom is the room in a law court where trials and hearings take place.
fact: In a UK courtroom, the judge may wear a wig, and a jury of twelve ordinary people listens to the evidence.
fact: Lawyers, witnesses and the person accused each have their own place in a courtroom.
fact: «Courtroom drama» means a story or TV show set in a courtroom.
fact: Schools may hold a mock trial in a pretend courtroom to learn how a trial works.
exercise: «Then we jump to a courtroom.» What is a courtroom? | A kind of wig worn by a judge | *A room in a law court where trials and hearings take place | A park with benches for the public | A room for cooking and baking
exercise: Which group of twelve ordinary people listens to the evidence in a courtroom? | The team | The choir | *The jury | The crew
exercise: «Every night Kai's house turned into a courtroom.» What does this tell you? | The house was a real law court | Kai was a judge in a real trial | The family moved to a new town | *The family was playing a pretend trial
test: Kai's family plays a pretend trial. Which word from «Every night at eight o'clock Kai's house turned into a courtroom» names the room? | house | *courtroom | eight | night
test: In a courtroom, who gives evidence about what they saw? | *The witness | The pilot | The gardener | The baker
exam: What is a «courtroom drama»? | A type of wig | *A story or TV show set in a courtroom | A game of football played in a park | A room for cooking
